{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/853610-indiana-jones-shenanigans","id":853610,"title":"Indiana Jones Shenanigans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-26T12:08:57-07:00","id":853610,"title":"Indiana Jones Shenanigans","content":"Is there any space in Beast for the tomb-robbing, temple investigating shenanigans that I loved so much about Mage? The main problem, I think, is that Beasts and their powers don't leave much of an impression on the physical world, not to mention the fact that aside from kinship there doesn't seem to be much incentive to seek out ancient knowledge. The only things I can think of off the top of my head are:<br /> <br /> - The possibility of finding the physical remains of an Incarnate (and possibly stopping mortal archaeologist from doing the same)<br /> - Finding out information on a very old Beast or Incarnate<br /> - Finding out the origins of an ancient Unfettered<br /> If anyone could come up with some interesting plotlines that would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-26-2016, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T13:53:19-07:00","id":853661,"title":"","content":"One of the settings (Lhasa, I think) introduces an artifact which may or may not be a body part of the Dark Mother. Maybe others are hidden in different parts of the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:02:31-07:00","id":853668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/853610-indiana-jones-shenanigans?p=853661#post853661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the settings (Lhasa, I think) introduces an artifact which may or may not be a body part of the Dark Mother. Maybe others are hidden in different parts of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>The severed claw, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:18:51-07:00","id":853673,"title":"","content":"Well you could allow beasts to learn new nightmares or Atavism for tomb robbing as a incentive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:24:37-07:00","id":853676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/853610-indiana-jones-shenanigans?p=853673#post853673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well you could allow beasts to learn new nightmares or Atavism for tomb robbing as a incentive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like the Word Walls from Elder Scrolls V:Skyrim?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:28:21-07:00","id":853679,"title":"","content":"If you really wanted to, I suppose you could come up with a Merit that lets Beasts into the parts of the Astral outside the Primordial Dream, with the option of disguising their Horror as another type of Goetia. In fact, since Skeleton Key is part of their template, Merits and Kinships with Mages might not be necessary. I know that spirits can diguise their relative Rank from other spirits when they want to avoid trouble, so maybe Horrors can do the same. You can use Skeleton Key to go dungeon crawling in the other Invisible Realms. The Hedge and the Underworld sound more appropriate for that than the Shadow. The Astral is a more case by case basis. YMMV, of course.<br /> <br /> As for tomb raiding in the mortal realm that focuses on other Beasts... you could borrow the idea of the Inamorata from Autumn Nightmares, or the Earthbound from Demon: The Fallen. Sometimes, when a True Fae, Incarnate or another epic monster dies for real, they leave behind parts of themselves that no longer possess a will, but can nonetheless cause some local rumors. Who knows, maybe if you find all the parts, you could bring them back/become the next one in their legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-26-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:49:05-07:00","id":853690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/853610-indiana-jones-shenanigans?p=853676#post853676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something like the Word Walls from Elder Scrolls V:Skyrim?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure why not what beast wouldn't want to obtain a nightmare from an incarnate or just an idea why not make an artifact that give an incarnate effect such as a mask that causes petrified gaze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T14:56:15-07:00","id":853692,"title":"","content":"Coming back to the idea of an Incarnate's corpse, what actually happens to an Incarnate if it dies in full monster-form? Does it sort of evaporate, leaving a human corpse? What I was thinking of was that it sort of mostly evaporates, leaving behind parts of its body that could carry on its Myth. Like the dragon's teeth that grew into soldiers or the heart of Fafnir that gave the ability to talk to animals when eaten. I must admit that I rather like the idea of an Incarnate's corpse becoming a kind of crystallised Myth, like the Noble Phantasms of the Heroic Spirits from Fate/Stay Night. <br /> <br /> I suppose that as artefacts the remains could be treated a little like Deathmasks from Geist. Perhaps each relic has its own power but acts subtly upon its user in order to further its Legend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:26:26-07:00","id":853707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/853610-indiana-jones-shenanigans?p=853692#post853692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Coming back to the idea of an Incarnate's corpse, what actually happens to an Incarnate if it dies in full monster-form? Does it sort of evaporate, leaving a human corpse? What I was thinking of was that it sort of mostly evaporates, leaving behind parts of its body that could carry on its Myth. Like the dragon's teeth that grew into soldiers or the heart of Fafnir that gave the ability to talk to animals when eaten. I must admit that I rather like the idea of an Incarnate's corpse becoming a kind of crystallised Myth, like the Noble Phantasms of the Heroic Spirits from Fate/Stay Night.<br /> <br /> I suppose that as artefacts the remains could be treated a little like Deathmasks from Geist. Perhaps each relic has its own power but acts subtly upon its user in order to further its Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div> A crystallized Myth also happens to Ascended Archmages. Their bodies become <i>Sariras</i>, items of power often composed of precious materials.<br /> <br /> So, if a Myth in item form can contain the powers of Incarnates...does that mean the Terror Mask from Splatterhouse could be such an item? I prefer the original version. It's minimal in dialogue and sounds properly heartless. The one from the remake speaks way too much and has a very human (if sadistic) attitude.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:38:09-07:00","id":853713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/853610-indiana-jones-shenanigans?p=853707#post853707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, if a Myth in item form can contain the powers of Incarnates...does that mean the Terror Mask from Splatterhouse could be such an item? I prefer the original version. It's minimal in dialogue and sounds properly heartless. The one from the remake speaks way too much and has a very human (if sadistic) attitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt that the relics would be as sentient and directly active as that but yes, probably. I was thinking that the Begotten are either immune to the curse or it basically gives them a second Legend while they are using it. For mortals, the relic's Legend temporarily replaces their Vice and the relic acts as a kind of 'back-seat conscience', subtly enticing them towards acting out the Legend. The relics would probably be very hard to permanently destroy (think of the One Ring) and don't tend to stay hidden for long. Some unlucky fool will find them in relatively short order. After all, how does a dragonbone sword continue the story when it's buried in the silt at the bottom of a bay?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:14:39-07:00","id":853838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/853610-indiana-jones-shenanigans#post853610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any space in Beast for the tomb-robbing, temple investigating shenanigans that I loved so much about Mage? The main problem, I think, is that Beasts and their powers don't leave much of an impression on the physical world, not to mention the fact that aside from kinship there doesn't seem to be much incentive to seek out ancient knowledge. (. . .)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, one of the chapter intros revolves around a Beast hanging out with a cabal of mages, doing a little tomb raiding . . .<br /> <br /> By pursuing the dark secrets of the world, a Beast can develop additional Nightmares reflecting the hidden horrors they uncover. The &quot;magic&quot; of Beasts, the lure of such new Nightmares offers plenty of reasons to explore lost temples to fallen gods, break into secret libraries of forbidden lore, hunt down exotic supernaturals or take tea with madmen. There's even a nice example of a Beast blackmailing a mummy with its Canopic jars. With each fell truth they learn, their Legend grows darker, scarring the human psyche deeper, making them ever stronger and better able to fend off Heroes . . .<br /> <br /> Collectors have even more reason to go dungeon crawling. They feed their Hunger by acquiring treasures precious to others - the rarer and more emotionally significant, the better the meal. The diary of an ancient vampire, lost for a thousand years, makes for a quite a feast. So would an Atlantean doomsday weapon, or an archmage's spell book. The design specs for the God-Machine, or secrets salvaged from Irem . . . A Collector builds its hoard one treasure at a time, and guards them like a jealous dragon (which makes such a hoard attractive to <i>other</i> Collectors . . . )<br /> <br /> Plus, there's good old-fashioned curiosity. Predators are often curious about the world around them, even if its only in a &quot;can I eat this&quot;-sense. And whatever else a Beast is, its a predator. Having caught a glimpse of the hidden world around them, why wouldn't they seek out more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 03-26-2016, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T23:38:54-07:00","id":853922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/853610-indiana-jones-shenanigans?p=853713#post853713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I doubt that the relics would be as sentient and directly active as that but yes, probably. I was thinking that the Begotten are either immune to the curse or it basically gives them a second Legend while they are using it. For mortals, the relic's Legend temporarily replaces their Vice and the relic acts as a kind of 'back-seat conscience', subtly enticing them towards acting out the Legend. The relics would probably be very hard to permanently destroy (think of the One Ring) and don't tend to stay hidden for long. Some unlucky fool will find them in relatively short order. After all, how does a dragonbone sword continue the story when it's buried in the silt at the bottom of a bay?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, these solidified Myths wouldn't really speak, per se. They would whisper into your soul now and then, pull a thread of fate here and there. Some would be more subtle than others. Of note is that Heroes could probably seek out these items as trophies or loot, and try to twist the Myth or Legend inside to their goals. Whether or not they'd be able to use them as effectively as Beasts is another story.<br /> <br /> I assume that the tendency to always be found somehow is a property of magic items in general, especially the cursed or just extremely coveted ones. The Props of the True Fae would be noteworthy in this regard, since these beings work through dream and fable logic. Unless you find out the Prop's mystical weakness, it'll always come back, and probably when you are most vulnerable or desperate.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Speaking of Beasts and magic items, it has been suggested that Conquering Heroes could include ways to facilitate the acquisition and use of magic items from other splats. Beasts could also take Goetia in the form of objects from the Astral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-27-2016, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:13:39-07:00","id":854940,"title":"","content":"Oh, and of course, there's always the added benefit of finding new and unique chambers to add to your Lair. What Beast wouldn't want their own private river of blood? Or a room full of (Dream animatronic) dark cultists, their eyes sewn shut, chanting hymns to inhuman gods in dead tongues? Who knows what kind of potential chambers you can find, when you're exploring the forgotten corners of the map.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:36:34-07:00","id":854947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/853610-indiana-jones-shenanigans?p=854940#post854940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and of course, there's always the added benefit of finding new and unique chambers to add to your Lair. What Beast wouldn't want their own private river of blood? Or a room full of (Dream animatronic) dark cultists, their eyes sewn shut, chanting hymns to inhuman gods in dead tongues? Who knows what kind of potential chambers you can find, when you're exploring the forgotten corners of the map.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd love to play a Cyber-Beast with a Tron-esque <b><a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/MinusWorld\" target=\"_blank\">Minus World</a></b> as a Chamber. It's hard to get much more off the map than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-29-2016, 05:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}